Wouldn't no-restricted-globals be more readable? `btoa` is already in the list of `no-restricted-globals`. In this case, it is not even a global. It's imported from `internalBinding('buffer').btoa`. Sounds good, let's add a comment explaining why we're not using no-restricted-globals then The second selector `CallExpression[callee.name='btoa']` is for case like:

```js
const { btoa } = internalBinding('buffer');
btoa('...');
``` Isn't transcode a better solution? The intent here is `string -> string`. `transcode` is `buffer -> buffer`, I don't see the advantage here with `transcode` like operation `string -> buffer transcode -> buffer -> string`, comparing to `string -> buffer -> string`. Ah, I see. Thanks! nit: I would put the comment inside the block (in case the block gets moved around, it's less likely to leave the comment behind), and I would specifically call out `no-restricted-globals` since that's what I was confused about.
