@jakecastelli Sounds good 👍 reordered the entries So `'node'` is incorrect performance entry type? @Semigradsky I think so, as pointed out from [this code snippet](https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/ca2ed88f94ca537c21a631cfecf577aa96afca0b/lib/internal/perf/observe.js#L88-L98), yet I'd like to double check on this.

@jakecastelli Could you please remove the 'author ready' to give me a bit of time to verify this? @Semigradsky Pretty sure the doc is outdated and `node` is no longer supported. It was firstly introduced [here](https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/67269fd7f33279699b1ae71225f3d738518c844c/lib/perf_hooks.js#L59C1-L65C3) and got removed in this [PR](https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/37136/files#diff-ce917fe2426ae73d71fe1dd18fea591589d849eb1e568d5fb653949f03fadc81L94:~:text=const%20observerableTypes%20%3D,%5D%3B) Ok, I see that we have [`PerformanceNodeTiming`](https://nodejs.org/docs/latest/api/perf_hooks.html#class-performancenodetiming) which extends [`PerformanceEntry`](https://nodejs.org/docs/latest/api/perf_hooks.html#class-performanceentry), and `entryType` for it can be `'node'` - https://github.com/jasnell/node/blob/262d0d0482ffd2fe7d654422df9df1f350045635/test/sequential/test-perf-hooks.js#L57

Base class can't be more narrow, so `entryType` can be 'node' for PerformanceEntry
 I overlooked that. I think you are right @Semigradsky after checking the implementation. Thank you for pointing it out. I have updated the PR

I think previously, this [PR](https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/37136/files#diff-ce917fe2426ae73d71fe1dd18fea591589d849eb1e568d5fb653949f03fadc81L94:~:text=const%20observerableTypes%20%3D,%5D%3B) did not remove the 'node' type but hide it as an unsupported one, [so that observer does not track it](https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/3cbeed88d9de9231f420ba53ad0e4d4a7af9c637/lib/internal/perf/observe.js#L298) Landed in e020dd8610978f752ff014b3d5558a3fadee69c9LGTM, one nit: shall we reorder them alphabetically?

e.g. 'dns', 'function', 'gc', 'http', ... LGTM

