  assert.ok(transfer instanceof StreamClass);
  
  const extended = class extends StreamClass {};
  const extendedOriginal = new extended();
  const extendedTransfer = structuredClone(extendedOriginal, { transfer: [extendedOriginal] });
  assert.strictEqual(Object.getPrototypeOf(extendedTransfer), StreamClass.prototype);
  assert.ok(extendedTransfer instanceof StreamClass);
}
``` @RedYetiDev Suggestion upon your suggestion. 😅 
```diff
  const extended = class extends StreamClass {};
- const extendedOriginal = new StreamClass();
+ const extendedOriginal = new extended();
``` sounds good. I noticed this was not exactly what the WPT was doing, so indeed updating it would be clearer. I did a rough benchmark, and it didn't show much perf improvement, but it's a good suggestion - putting it in constructor is more proper. by "rough", I mean 😅
```js
console.time('1')
for (let i = 0; i < 10_000; i++) {
  const r1 = new ReadableStream(); 
  structuredClone(r1, { transfer: [r1] });
  
  const w1 = new WritableStream();
  structuredClone(w1, { transfer: [w1] });
  
  const t1 = new TransformStream();
  structuredClone(t1, { transfer: [t1] });
}
console.timeEnd('1')
```

Comparing this with the suggested changes, I don't see much difference. A benchmark CI summary would be more accurate I think.

