Optional chaining x 103,663,582 ops/sec ±6.25% (75 runs sampled)
Without optional chaining x 106,320,156 ops/sec ±5.14% (76 runs sampled)
Fastest is Without optional chaining,Optional chaining
``` ahh interesting. In that case, then yes, this is purely cosmetic, but I still think that using optional chaining is more concise and readable than without, but if it adds too much noise, it's not a **needed** change, however I'd love to see some other opinions. ## [Codecov](https://app.codecov.io/gh/nodejs/node/pull/55045?dropdown=coverage&src=pr&el=h1&utm_medium=referral&utm_source=github&utm_content=comment&utm_campaign=pr+comments&utm_term=nodejs) Report
