Can you please spell out these single-character variable names? We might remove `--experimental-loader` in the future. Can we write this test with `--import` and `register` instead? You can pass a data URL to both `--import` and `register`, so it’s still possible to keep all the fixtures within this file. You can see an example at https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/fba2c9332f4bccc2b0b300de234d413ae28b4b9c/test/es-module/test-esm-import-assertion-warning.mjs. I followed the precedent from the test above. I think I should do that holistically in different PR. Also followed precedent here. Can do this in a separate PR. This doesn't feel like a separate PR concern. The precedent is just because most of the loader tests are old, before the design change. Let's not add more tests that are hard to decipher. Just because some other test isn't as legible as it can be doesn't mean we should add another one. Changing `--loader` to `--import` seems like a refactor that addresses a separate issue related to outdated tests.

I'm willing to handle it, but I'd prefer to approach it comprehensively and update all tests using `--loader`. This would go beyond the specific problem that this pull request is addressing.
 Same response: https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/51033#discussion_r1414826453 If you’d like to do a follow-up to update all the old tests to use the new style, that would be great. Lately we’ve been focusing on using the new style for _new_ tests, to at least not dig our hole any deeper. Updated! Sorry for being difficult, but I think we should keep the hook in the test file, as using an external file makes it harder to follow IMO
